      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/chalkhill_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Downer Tavern, built ~1826, served as post office 1956‑1985, becoming a community hub before the new post office opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/chalkhill_pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Chalk Hill sits on the National Road (Route 40), 8 miles southeast of Uniontown, in the Laurel Highlands.",
